The branch `kimi/6767-deviceid-crash` already exists. Now implement the fix in `getDeviceId()`: wrap get/set in try/catch, with a module-level fallback id so that a blocked localStorage doesn't produce a new random id every call (stability within session). Keep it minimal and consistent with file style (console.warn like writeLocalCustomSetsAllInternal).

Implementation:

```ts
let sessionFallbackDeviceId: string | null = null;

export function getDeviceId(): string {
  if (typeof window === 'undefined') return 'server_ssr';
  try {
    let deviceId = localStorage.getItem(DEVICE_ID_KEY);
    if (!deviceId) {
      deviceId = sessionFallbackDeviceId ?? `dev_${Math.random().toString(36).substring(2, 11)}_${Date.now()}`;
      sessionFallbackDeviceId = deviceId;
      localStorage.setItem(DEVICE_ID_KEY, deviceId);
    }
    return deviceId;
  } catch (err) {
    console.warn('localStorage unavailable; using session-scoped device id', err);
    if (!sessionFallbackDeviceId) {
      sessionFallbackDeviceId = `dev_${Math.random().toString(36).substring(2, 11)}_${Date.now()}`;
    }
    return sessionFallbackDeviceId;
  }
}
```

Hmm, subtle: if getItem succeeds and returns null but setItem throws, we'd generate a new id each call unless we cache it before setItem. Caching sessionFallbackDeviceId before setItem covers that. Keep it simple.

Actually simpler:

```ts
let inMemoryDeviceId: string | null = null;

function newDeviceId(): string {
  if (!inMemoryDeviceId) {
    inMemoryDeviceId = `dev_${Math.random().toString(36).substring(2, 11)}_${Date.now()}`;
  }
  return inMemoryDeviceId;
}

export function getDeviceId(): string {
  if (typeof window === 'undefined') return 'server_ssr';
  try {
    const stored = localStorage.getItem(DEVICE_ID_KEY);
    if (stored) return stored;
    const deviceId = newDeviceId();
    localStorage.setItem(DEVICE_ID_KEY, deviceId);
    return deviceId;
  } catch (err) {
    console.warn('localStorage unavailable; using in-memory device id', err);
    return newDeviceId();
  }
}
```

This is clean and minimal. saveLocalCustomSet and deleteLocalCustomSet then can't throw from getDeviceId; writeLocalCustomSetsAllInternal already catches.

Now tests: add a new test file or extend? The issue says "Test: mock localStorage.setItem to throw; creating a custom set does not throw" and verification runs `npx vitest run tests/unit/custom-decks-membership.test.ts` plus a new storage-failure case. I'll create `site/tests/unit/custom-decks-storage-failure.test.ts` (new file) so existing tests aren't weakened.

Test needs a browser-ish environment. Check how other tests handle localStorage — LexiconPractice.test.tsx probably uses jsdom. Check vitest config.

